  "text": "The cluricaune is a Scottish and Irish being. Unlike the busy leprechaun, this solitary fairy liked to lounge and to dress with care. He wore silver-buckled shoes, a cap with golden lace, and a suit of red, the color of the Solitary Fairy. Fond of strong drink, he stole into wine cellars to lift bottles. He was hard to expel, for he rode away inside a cask. Folk in Co. Cork used this name, while nearby areas gave him other names. One such being, named Little Wildbeam, helped a Quaker family in Cork by saving every drop of beer from a cask.",
